he 5 s local budget unchanged: it runs after a read() of that same tip, which has already materialized the object locally.'","set_gate (line 683-686) calls _cas_advance after only _ref_oid, with no _read_blob_bytes; set_pause create-path similar. Only acquire/renew/try_break_if_stale read the blob before _cas_advance.","_cas_advance line 510 calls _object_type(repo_root, old_oid) which on a blobless clone could lazily fetch a legacy blob tip."],"finding":"The plan's rationale for leaving _cas_advance's _object_type probe at the 5s LOCAL budget ('it runs after a read() of that same tip, which has already materialized the object locally') does not hold for all _cas_advance callers: set_gate and set_pause create/update paths call _cas_advance after only _ref_oid, with no prior blob read, so on a blobless clone a legacy blob tip could make that probe a lazy fetch that times out at 5s.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fac29e2e15579e179","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach section ('_cas_advance ... keeps the 5 s local budget unchanged: it runs after a read() of that same tip'); src/rebar/reconciler/_ref_lock.py lines 510, 683-686, 764-776","norm_id":"n0e857ba850f32035","priority":0.8,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A blobless CI clone performs a gate set (set_gate) or pause (set_pause) whose current tip is a legacy blob that is not local — the _object_type(old_oid) probe in _cas_advance lazily fetches and risks the same 5s timeout the plan is fixing on the read path."],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Either narrow the rationale to the read path only (acquire/renew/steal legitimately materialize the tip first), and explicitly note that set_gate/set_pause legacy-blob tips are out of scope because legacy blob tips only arise from rebar<=0.13 git remotes that are not blobless-cloned; or give _cas_advance's probe the remote budget too for symmetry.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.8,"verification":{"binary":{"a